
v0.6.0:
 - Breaking: the default control socket directory is `/run/vey-keyless` for root on Linux and `/var/run/vey-keyless` for root on other Unix systems; another Linux user uses an absolute `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` or `/run/user/<uid>/vey-keyless`
 - BUG FIX: a buffered stream copy or vectored write stops when the writer returns no bytes
 - BUG FIX: a Fluentd handshake reports a closed connection instead of parsing a short HELO or PONG
 - BUG FIX: a large Linux journald record can be sealed and sent
 - BUG FIX: a non-ASCII size string in worker or statsd config is rejected instead of panicking
 - BUG FIX: a relative pid file is created in the working directory from before daemonizing, and the lock is held until the process exits
 - BUG FIX: a rotating histogram still publishes while samples keep arriving, and `0.0` and `-0.0` count as one quantile
 - BUG FIX: a TLS Fluentd client finishes the forward handshake after TLS, and an unknown HELO option is rejected
 - BUG FIX: an empty daemon group uses `_.sock` as the control socket
 - BUG FIX: an incomplete legacy rustls certificate pair fails config load instead of being ignored
 - BUG FIX: an issued certificate cannot start before its issuer, and its `pathlen` cannot exceed what the issuer allows
 - BUG FIX: certificate times outside 1950-2049 use GeneralizedTime, and a timestamp offset that includes seconds is written in UTC
 - BUG FIX: on Windows, another control client can connect while one connection is still open
 - BUG FIX: OpenSSL async engine file descriptors are registered with the I/O-safe AsyncFd API
 - BUG FIX: the crypto_mb backend reduces an ECDSA digest modulo the curve order, and uses OpenSSL when that value is zero
 - BUG FIX: the crypto_mb backend rejects an RSA-PSS digest that is not the hash length
 - BUG FIX: the register keepalive request is a complete HTTP header
 - BUG FIX: the Windows hostname sent to syslog and Fluentd no longer includes a trailing NUL
 - Feature: support multiple server types, selected with the `type` key in each server config
     - `cloudflare`: the Cloudflare Keyless server, which is the default type if `type` is omitted
     - `plain_tcp_port`: a plain TCP port that forwards accepted connections to the `server` it points to
     - `plain_tls_port`: a TLS port backed by rustls, which terminates TLS and forwards the stream to the `server` it points to
 - Feature: `listen` is now optional in a `cloudflare` server, so it can serve only the connections sent by port servers
 - Feature: port servers support the PROXY Protocol via `proxy_protocol` and `proxy_protocol_read_timeout`
 - Feature: `server` references are verified when the config is loaded, so a missing or self-referencing next server is rejected at startup
 - Feature: optional `crypto_mb` backend (feature `crypto-mb`, x86_64 only) using Intel crypto_mb for batched RSA-2048/3072/4096, ECDSA P-256/P-384/P-521, and Ed25519; single-request batches fall back to OpenSSL
 - Feature: dispatch Ed25519 private-key operations to worker backends
 - Compatibility: bump MSRV to 1.94.0
 - Compatibility: DragonFly worker `sched_affinity` applies to the calling thread

v0.5.0:
 - BUG FIX: enforce async-op timeout inside OpensslAsyncTask (`vey-openssl`); on timeout return a cleanup handle so the error response can be sent before draining the in-flight ASYNC_JOB (avoids job-pool leaks under load)
 - BUG FIX: count async-job crypto failures with `add_by_error_code` instead of always incrementing passed, so success metrics are not inflated on encrypt/sign failures
 - Feature: reload the running process via RPC/ctl (`reload`) without a full restart
 - Feature: support set TCP max segment size in listen config
 - Feature: local key store file watching (inotify) also works on FreeBSD
 - Feature: optional jemalloc or mimalloc global allocator at compile time; allocator name/version appear in `--version`
 - Feature: derive default config / log / metrics / controller names from the binary name (supports renamed installs)
 - Feature: `--version` reports the OpenSSL variant actually linked
 - Compatibility: bump MSRV to 1.91.0

v0.4.4:
 - Feature: allow to set tcp keepalive on tcp listen socket in server

v0.4.3:
 - Feature: restore support for aws-lc
 - Feature: add support for aws-lc-fips
 - Deprecated: the following config options are deprecated:
     - emit_duration in statsd config, use emit_interval instead

v0.4.2:
 - Feature: allow to read symlink files on local store dir
 - Feature: allow to retry register on startup
 - Feature: add cli options to allow quit on panic
 - Feature: allow to enable tls usage in server
 - Feature: add more fields to request log

v0.4.1:
 - Feature: allow to set openssl async job size in worker config
 - Feature: allow to set worker CPU affinity from environment variables

v0.4.0:
 - Feature: add worker support, and also allow to use multiple threads in main runtime
 - Compatibility: drop AWS-LC support to reduce outdated dependencies

v0.3.5:
 - Feature: emit tokio runtime metrics
 - Feature: allow to send event logs to stdout
 - Optimization: more robust daemon hot restart

v0.3.4:
 - Feature: add more error types to request log
 - Feature: emit request duration stats
 - Feature: disable openssl-async-job by default
 - BUG FIX: fix logger io stats

v0.3.3:
 - Feature: allow to check key existence via g3keymess-ctl
 - BUG FIX: fix auto load of newly added keys in the local store dir

v0.3.2:
 - BUG FIX: fix sign action
 - BUG FIX: add missing request tags for gauge metrics
 - Optimization: ignore early connection close error
 - Feature: various improvements to journal logging
     - add SYSLOG_IDENTIFIER field
     - improved efficiency
     - io stats added
 - Feature: drop out of date dependencies by using forks and patches

v0.3.1:
 - Feature: default to guess main config file when run as systemd service
 - BUG FIX: ignore failure of ExecStop to ensure restart on success

v0.3.0:
 - Feature: allow to register service before running
 - Feature: always restart after service success quit
 - Feature: add the following global rpc methods:
     - add_metrics_tag to add metrics tag to all metrics
     - list_keys to list SKI of all stored keys

v0.2.0:
 - Initial release
